      "content": "First, conduct a thorough investigation to detect signs of tampering, focusing on unusual entry points, severed wires, altered settings, or added obstructions within the reefer unit. Consult with security personnel to examine the site and review surveillance footage for observations. Reach out to the service company that recently maintained the unit for a comprehensive review of their service and work performed. Cooperate with marine engineers to analyze internal system functionality, evaluating both software and hardware aspects. Notify relevant authorities if sabotage is suspected. Review and tighten security procedures and access controls. Develop a comprehensive root-cause analysis with the supplier and manufacturer to discern the cause of the failure. As a contingency plan, confirm availability with alternative transportation means and manage customer expectations efficiently. Document all findings meticulously, and communicate transparently with all stakeholders involved. As the incident requires broader investigation and investigation of potential sabotage still ongoing, lessons learned should be documented and used to reinforce future protocols and preventive measures, ensuring system resilience and readiness.",
